The following code snippet contains a bug:

```php
    private function findEndOfNextBlock(Tokens $tokens, $index)
    {
        $index = $tokens->getNextTokenOfKind($index, ['{']);

        return $tokens->findBlockEnd(Tokens::BLOCK_TYPE_CURLY_BRACE, $index);
    }
```

The code fails the following tests:

Test `PhpCsFixer\Tests\Fixer\PhpUnit\PhpUnitTestCaseStaticMethodCallsFixerTest::testFix with data set "do not crash on abstract static function"`:
            
```php
    public function testFix($expected, $input = null, array $config = [])
    {
        $this->fixer->configure($config);
        $this->doTest($expected, $input);
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Illegal offset type
```

Please provide a fixed version of the buggy function, and only that function without additional imports. Make sure the code is between ``` and ```.
```php
    private function findEndOfNextBlock(Tokens $tokens, $index)
    {
        $openingBraceIndex = $tokens->getNextTokenOfKind($index, ['{']);
        if (null === $openingBraceIndex) {
            return null; // or handle the case where no opening brace is found
        }

        return $tokens->findBlockEnd(Tokens::BLOCK_TYPE_CURLY_BRACE, $openingBraceIndex);
    }
```
